1
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:09,360
Looking down from the sky, I don't even have to guess.
I know you're smiling, Fun.

2
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:15,270
My life now is probably exactly the way you've always wanted it to be, isn't it?

3
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:37,800
Every day I get to spend with P'Fah makes me so happy.

4
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:41,780
Sometimes it feels so perfect that I have to pinch myself when I wake up.

5
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:43,690
Good morning.

6
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:49,560
I'm starting to lose track of whether this is a dream or reality.

7
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:51,700
Even though it's been quite a while,

8
00:00:52,110 --> 00:00:54,210
P'Fah is still the same.

9
00:00:54,390 --> 00:00:56,550
Everything about him is still the same.

10
00:00:56,930 --> 00:00:59,840
And he's still the sky for me.

11
00:01:05,790 --> 00:01:09,130
P'Fah is practically a full-time businessman now.

12
00:01:09,430 --> 00:01:12,790
He moved to Bangkok to manage the hospital's new branch.

13
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,350
As for me,

14
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:42,690
besides doing my best to take care of P'Fah,

15
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:46,220
I'm officially a professional photographer now.

16
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:22,510
But there's something I need to tell about him.

17
00:02:22,690 --> 00:02:24,890
Even though P'Fah is a light sleeper,

18
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:26,780
he always pretends to be asleep

19
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:29,910
just so I'll wake him up with a kiss on the cheek every morning.

20
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:40,900
First photo of the day,

21
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:44,970
still as cute as ever.

22
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:51,090
You have a meeting at 11:30 today.

23
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:55,040
And you have a block-shot with the studio at 10:00.

24
00:02:58,110 --> 00:03:00,810
Look at you using technical words now.

25
00:03:01,230 --> 00:03:04,220
P'Fah, you're the best in the world.

26
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:06,880
Just a little.

27
00:03:06,970 --> 00:03:09,830
I had to keep up with my boyfriend.

28
00:03:15,370 --> 00:03:17,300
So that means

29
00:03:17,710 --> 00:03:21,390
our schedules line up today. We don't have to go separately.

30
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:25,420
So let me drive you to work first, okay?

31
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:29,050
Our schedules seem to line up almost every day now.

32
00:03:29,470 --> 00:03:34,940
It's like you secretly matched your schedule to mine.

33
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:38,130
Uh... well...

34
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:40,810
I mean...

35
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:45,500
I knew it.

36
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:49,330
I'm a terrible liar, you know that.

37
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:56,340
What can I do? I just don't want to be away from my boyfriend for too long.

38
00:03:56,790 --> 00:04:00,450
If I could, I'd drive you everywhere, every single day.

39
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:02,480
Anywhere in the world.

40
00:04:05,170 --> 00:04:08,080
Oh, I see.

41
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:10,930
Is that why you still won't teach me how to drive?

42
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:14,700
That's right.

43
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,550
P'Fah...

44
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:23,560
If you keep scolding me, I'm going to tease you.

45
00:04:24,850 --> 00:04:25,910
But...

46
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:30,480
I haven't—

47
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:42,800
I have to get to work now.

48
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:45,800
I'm going to be late. See you later, Phoon.

49
00:05:00,490 --> 00:05:01,700
What's that smile for, little one?

50
00:05:03,870 --> 00:05:05,160
Just go.

51
00:05:08,550 --> 00:05:11,850
Fun, how many times can I fall in love with the same person?

52
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:42,880
Thank you.

53
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:46,880
I'll call you when my meeting's over.

54
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,980
Work hard, okay?

55
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:54,360
Phoon.

56
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:58,500
I miss you already.

57
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:03,400
Miss me? You haven't even left yet.

58
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:07,290
I'm just saying it in advance. I'll miss you the moment I drive away.

59
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:11,420
Go to work already.

60
00:06:11,630 --> 00:06:13,700
But I still have a little time left.

61
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:16,370
- Give it a try. I can wait a little longer.
- No.

62
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:18,630
You'll be late for work.

63
00:06:23,850 --> 00:06:24,860
Okay.

64
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:27,110
Then have a good day at work.

65
00:06:27,290 --> 00:06:28,420
Bye.

66
00:06:28,970 --> 00:06:30,330
Come back soon.

67
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,100
Good morning.

68
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:58,550
Morning. And this too.

69
00:06:59,850 --> 00:07:02,550
Take a close look and let me know what you think.

70
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:05,880
Sure. Just leave it over there.

71
00:07:06,670 --> 00:07:10,240
P'Fah's boyfriend is even smaller than that bag. So adorable.

72
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:13,140
Phoon.

73
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,160
Phoon.

74
00:07:20,070 --> 00:07:24,280
So, is P'Fah's boyfriend ready to work?

75
00:07:25,690 --> 00:07:27,440
- Good morning.
- Morning.

76
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:28,620
- Yes.
- Well, well.

77
00:07:32,070 --> 00:07:33,710
- This way.
- Okay.

78
00:07:35,410 --> 00:07:38,490
Love really does change people.

79
00:07:38,570 --> 00:07:41,640
- This is the look we're shooting, right?
- Yep, that's the one.

80
00:07:46,070 --> 00:07:47,180
Okay.

81
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:50,920
Alright, that's a wrap for today.

82
00:08:14,170 --> 00:08:16,030
It's already 4:00?

83
00:08:17,590 --> 00:08:19,090
Little one.

84
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,360
P'Fah.

85
00:09:31,510 --> 00:09:32,780
Little one.

86
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:35,200
When did you fall asleep here?

87
00:09:41,090 --> 00:09:43,550
Hey, that's not good.

88
00:09:49,530 --> 00:09:51,030
Since 2:00 this afternoon.

89
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:55,570
You were in a meeting and looked stressed, so I waited for you.

90
00:09:55,730 --> 00:09:58,360
I don't even know when I dozed off.

91
00:09:59,270 --> 00:10:00,240
Really?

92
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:05,700
My meeting just ended too. I was so worried because you weren't answering your phone.

93
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:09,880
Turns out you were sleeping here looking all adorable.

94
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:15,150
Have you been in meetings since this morning?

95
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,460
Did you even get a lunch break?

96
00:10:32,630 --> 00:10:35,840
Something urgent came up, so I had to go through.

97
00:10:44,990 --> 00:10:46,840
Aren't you pushing yourself too hard?

98
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:52,600
That's just how it is when you're starting out.

99
00:10:54,290 --> 00:10:58,480
Things should get better once everything settles down.

100
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:03,430
Now that you're fully in charge,

101
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:05,910
Don't you want to go back to treating patients?

102
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:10,210
I do.

103
00:11:11,410 --> 00:11:12,830
But I think

104
00:11:13,090 --> 00:11:15,160
I want to see this through first.

105
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:17,400
Once everything's settled,

106
00:11:17,810 --> 00:11:19,360
then I'll go back.

107
00:11:24,380 --> 00:11:26,750
If we hadn't had to move here,

108
00:11:27,370 --> 00:11:29,880
you wouldn't have to work this hard.

109
00:11:41,110 --> 00:11:42,550
Why would you say that?

110
00:11:42,900 --> 00:11:46,220
I know this move wasn't part of your first plan.

111
00:11:47,090 --> 00:11:49,170
It wasn't what you had planned.

112
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:51,900
It's because of

113
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:54,850
my work.

114
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:59,700
Am I making you work too hard?

115
00:12:00,990 --> 00:12:04,000
It hurts me to hear you say that, little one.

116
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:06,990
It's like you don't believe in my love for you.

117
00:12:07,530 --> 00:12:10,870
No, that's not what I mean. I never thought that.

118
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:13,460
I'm just genuinely worried about you.

119
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:19,840
I don't want you to sacrifice yourself

120
00:12:20,550 --> 00:12:22,600
or give up who you are for me.

121
00:12:26,670 --> 00:12:30,890
But for everything you just said, I'd gladly give it all up.

122
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,090
P'Fah...

123
00:12:34,290 --> 00:12:35,560
You know,

124
00:12:36,180 --> 00:12:37,760
I never really had a dream

125
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:39,830
or anything I truly wanted to do.

126
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:44,700
I just lived the life my parents wanted for me.

127
00:12:47,370 --> 00:12:49,050
Then you came into my life,

128
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:51,880
and I finally understood what life means.

129
00:12:53,230 --> 00:12:54,170
Phoon,

130
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:58,000
let me make every day of your life a good one.

131
00:12:59,050 --> 00:13:00,840
Because every time you smile,

132
00:13:01,420 --> 00:13:03,520
that's my happiness.

133
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:13,610
I'm sorry for bringing this up.

134
00:13:13,850 --> 00:13:16,600
I ended up making you feel uneasy.

135
00:13:18,990 --> 00:13:21,080
I've never doubted you.

136
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:25,330
I'm just really worried about you.

137
00:13:26,250 --> 00:13:27,560
It's okay.

138
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:31,360
How about this?

139
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:34,450
I'll manage my time better.

140
00:13:34,790 --> 00:13:37,860
I'll eat on time and get enough sleep.

141
00:13:38,450 --> 00:13:39,370
Deal?

142
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:40,920
Deal.

143
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:46,520
How about I support you instead?

144
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:47,830
Huh?

145
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:48,890
Mm-hmm.

146
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:55,680
Why not? I have a job, and I make good money.

147
00:13:55,810 --> 00:13:57,610
I can easily take care of you.

148
00:13:57,730 --> 00:14:00,630
I want you to retire and stay home,

149
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:03,260
please? Let me take care of you.

150
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:06,490
Retire?

151
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:09,890
I'm not that old. I'm still young.

152
00:14:10,070 --> 00:14:14,140
You worked hard through school,
and now you're working even harder.

153
00:14:14,970 --> 00:14:17,850
You've never really had the chance to live an easy life like everyone else.

154
00:14:21,140 --> 00:14:22,770
Thank you for worrying about me.

155
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:26,210
Then I promise I won't push myself too hard.

156
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:30,000
And if one day I really can't keep going,
I'll quit right away

157
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:32,240
and stay home so you can take care of me.

158
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:50,520
Is something wrong?

159
00:14:51,690 --> 00:14:52,950
Phoon.

160
00:14:53,410 --> 00:14:57,790
Are those Prae and Fai, the ones you showed me in your photos?

161
00:15:20,890 --> 00:15:22,300
Your name is Pha Fai?

162
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,950
That's such a cute name.

163
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:28,280
Yes, but Mom says you can just call me Fai.

164
00:15:29,110 --> 00:15:31,050
Well, my name is Tonfah.

165
00:15:31,310 --> 00:15:33,170
You can just call me P'Fah.

166
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:38,640
Okay, P'Fah. What are you doing at the hospital today?

167
00:15:38,690 --> 00:15:40,000
Are you sick?

168
00:15:40,890 --> 00:15:43,490
I'm a doctor. I'm here to take care of sick people.

169
00:15:43,750 --> 00:15:50,160
Then can you take care of my mommy too?
Another doctor said she's sick.

170
00:15:56,310 --> 00:15:57,270
Of course.

171
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:06,370
Fai is usually very afraid of strangers.

172
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:10,350
But somehow she gets along really well with that doctor.

173
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:11,630
How strange.

174
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,620
P'Tonfah is a psychiatrist.

175
00:16:16,050 --> 00:16:18,040
He probably knows how to connect with children.

176
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,960
But you still haven't told me,

177
00:16:24,330 --> 00:16:26,100
why you're at the hospital, Aunt Prae.

178
00:16:30,390 --> 00:16:32,790
They found a small lump.

179
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:34,890
A lump?

180
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:38,300
But the doctor said there's no need to worry yet.

181
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:42,040
It could just be a benign lump.

182
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:43,910
Nothing dangerous.

183
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:47,520
So... when will you know the results?

184
00:16:48,290 --> 00:16:52,780
I was actually supposed to be admitted today for a biopsy.

185
00:16:53,570 --> 00:16:56,790
But I asked to postpone the appointment.

186
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,860
Why did you postpone it?

187
00:17:00,150 --> 00:17:02,520
Wouldn't it be better to find out as soon as possible?

188
00:17:05,590 --> 00:17:07,350
You're that worried about me?

189
00:17:09,980 --> 00:17:12,430
I only postponed it for six days.

190
00:17:13,210 --> 00:17:17,760
Fai's grandmother is overseas on an important trip.

191
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:20,960
If I have to be admitted,

192
00:17:21,360 --> 00:17:23,450
I'm worried there won't be anyone to look after her.

193
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:26,450
So I have to wait until Grandma comes back.

194
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:30,650
But...

195
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:34,010
Six days is still a long time.

196
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,150
What else can I do?

197
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:39,710
I don't trust anyone else to take care of her.

198
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:44,250
I'll help.

199
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:47,690
The green one.

200
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:56,300
What if it wasn't just anyone... but her big brother?

201
00:17:56,840 --> 00:17:58,380
Would you be okay with that?

202
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:11,640
But...

203
00:18:12,350 --> 00:18:14,600
You could ask Fai first.

204
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:19,340
Maybe it'll help you get examined sooner.

205
00:18:20,970 --> 00:18:22,240
Thank you.

206
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:24,450
I'll ask her.

207
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:28,820
If she's okay with it, I might have to trouble you two.

208
00:18:36,910 --> 00:18:38,840
What are you drawing?

209
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:41,120
- Need a hand?
- Sure.

210
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:49,150
Fai, it's time to go home.

211
00:18:57,460 --> 00:19:00,690
Have you thanked them yet? They must be exhausted from playing with you.

212
00:19:00,920 --> 00:19:02,830
Thank you, P'Fah.

213
00:19:03,170 --> 00:19:04,450
P'Phoon.

214
00:19:06,650 --> 00:19:08,160
Let's play again sometime.

215
00:19:09,710 --> 00:19:11,240
We'll get going now.

216
00:19:11,410 --> 00:19:12,330
Okay.

217
00:19:12,730 --> 00:19:14,320
- Bye.
- Goodbye.

218
00:19:14,630 --> 00:19:17,300
- Bye-bye, Fai.
- Bye-bye.

219
00:19:18,050 --> 00:19:20,700
Take care.

220
00:19:21,290 --> 00:19:22,060
Let's go.

221
00:19:33,570 --> 00:19:34,480
P'Fah.

222
00:19:50,780 --> 00:19:52,130
Your coffee, P'Fah.

223
00:19:52,540 --> 00:19:53,470
Thank you.

224
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:58,180
Phoon.

225
00:19:59,180 --> 00:20:02,610
I've received a summary of Aunt Prae's medical records.

226
00:20:05,310 --> 00:20:06,600
How is she?

227
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:09,730
Just like she said.

228
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:12,960
We'll have to wait for the biopsy results.

229
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:18,840
Are you worried about her?

230
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:26,440
I just wish she could get the results sooner.

231
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:29,060
But according to her records,

232
00:20:29,400 --> 00:20:31,480
she postponed the appointment until next week.

233
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:34,930
That's right.

234
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:38,190
She said there's no one to look after Fai.

235
00:20:38,950 --> 00:20:41,950
She has to wait until Fai's grandmother returns from overseas next week.

236
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:52,500
Phoon.

237
00:21:00,520 --> 00:21:02,030
Yes, Aunt Prae.

238
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:11,660
Of course.

239
00:21:13,090 --> 00:21:15,850
Tomorrow works. I'm free anyway.

240
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:22,880
I'll send you the location later.

241
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:25,650
Goodbye.

242
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:33,120
P'Fah.

243
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,400
Let's babysit.

244
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:36,600
Huh?

245
00:21:40,850 --> 00:21:43,560
Are you sure you'll be okay staying with them?

246
00:21:43,660 --> 00:21:44,980
Yes.

247
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:50,550
Don't be naughty, don't run around, and listen to them, okay?

248
00:21:50,830 --> 00:21:52,410
Okay, Mommy.

249
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:55,710
Aunt Prae.

250
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:59,190
Is Fai allergic to anything or unable to eat anything?

251
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:03,010
No. She'll eat anything delicious.

252
00:22:03,430 --> 00:22:04,480
Right?

253
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:10,080
That's perfect. P'Phoon is an amazing cook.

254
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:14,180
If there's anything you want to eat, just tell P'Phoon.

255
00:22:14,580 --> 00:22:15,950
Okay.

256
00:22:16,820 --> 00:22:19,940
Aunt Prae, it's almost time for your appointment.

257
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:22,020
- Let's go. I'll take you there.
- Okay.

258
00:22:22,350 --> 00:22:23,530
Mommy's leaving now.

259
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:30,990
Let's see what toys you brought.

260
00:22:31,120 --> 00:22:32,090
Here.

261
00:22:32,450 --> 00:22:34,250
What a cute bag.

262
00:22:34,670 --> 00:22:36,830
- Can I open it?
- Sure.

263
00:22:39,740 --> 00:22:41,690
You're look exactly alike.

264
00:22:51,890 --> 00:22:54,930
Once you arrive at the hospital, just tell them my name.

265
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:57,740
A nurse will be assigned to take special care of you.

266
00:22:57,860 --> 00:22:59,980
The biopsy results should be ready within three days.

267
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:05,480
You can stay at the hospital in the meantime.
It'll be more convenient, and you'll be close to the doctors.

268
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:08,360
When I first met Typhoon,

269
00:23:08,650 --> 00:23:10,180
he wasn't cheerful at all.

270
00:23:10,860 --> 00:23:15,400
But seeing him again now,
everything has changed.

271
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:20,480
Typhoon is lucky to have someone as wonderful as Tonfah taking care of him.

272
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:26,060
No, we're all the lucky ones to have found each other.

273
00:23:27,260 --> 00:23:28,730
Please take good care of Fai.

274
00:23:30,350 --> 00:23:33,840
Don't worry.
We'll take good care of both Fai and your treatment.

275
00:23:34,120 --> 00:23:37,080
All the doctors and nurses will do their very best.

276
00:23:37,990 --> 00:23:41,920
Tonfah, you almost make me think you own this hospital.

277
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:46,190
Uh...

278
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:50,590
- Anyway, have a safe trip.
- Thank you.

279
00:24:04,350 --> 00:24:06,530
I finished putting it together. Like this?

280
00:24:06,660 --> 00:24:08,840
That's right. It's a hamburger.

281
00:24:08,890 --> 00:24:10,030
Oh.

282
00:24:11,410 --> 00:24:14,480
What's this? Oh, it's an ice cream.

283
00:24:20,710 --> 00:24:21,860
Fai.

284
00:24:23,060 --> 00:24:24,900
Go ask P'Fah to come play with us.

285
00:24:26,780 --> 00:24:27,640
Okay.

286
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:32,740
- P'Fah.
- Yes?

287
00:24:32,910 --> 00:24:35,440
Would you like to play with us? I brought lots of toys.

288
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:37,170
Sure.

289
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:38,020
Let's go.

290
00:24:38,670 --> 00:24:39,880
Come on.

291
00:24:48,300 --> 00:24:50,240
Now then,

292
00:24:50,410 --> 00:24:52,050
what shall we play today?

293
00:24:52,660 --> 00:24:54,100
How about playing house?

294
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:58,100
P'Fah will be the dad, P'Phoon will be the mom, and I'll be the child.

295
00:25:00,830 --> 00:25:01,920
Sure.

296
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:04,720
Is that okay, Phoon?

297
00:25:05,500 --> 00:25:07,130
Uh... sure.

298
00:25:08,180 --> 00:25:11,790
So, what would you like to eat today, sweetheart?

299
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:15,680
- I want a hamburger. Can you make one for me?
- A hamburger?

300
00:25:15,950 --> 00:25:20,550
Of course. Papa will make one for you himself.

301
00:25:20,980 --> 00:25:22,790
Does Mama want one too?

302
00:25:23,390 --> 00:25:25,450
Oh, Mama wants one too.

303
00:25:25,610 --> 00:25:28,580
Okay, let's start with...

304
00:25:30,430 --> 00:25:32,070
Oh, it lives in the ground.

305
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,660
In the ground? A millipede?

306
00:25:33,990 --> 00:25:35,150
- It has spikes.
- Right.

307
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:36,590
Spikes? A cactus?

308
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:38,020
It's a mammal...

309
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:39,290
A giraffe?

310
00:25:39,510 --> 00:25:41,120
Skip, skip.

311
00:25:42,100 --> 00:25:45,160
Time's up! Yay!

312
00:25:45,910 --> 00:25:48,320
I've never seen a stork in my life.

313
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:50,840
I just found out it has an orange beak.

314
00:25:54,540 --> 00:25:57,410
P'Fah, you have to be the evil witch.

315
00:25:57,830 --> 00:26:00,590
Fai, let's run! The evil witch is coming to catch us!

316
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:03,340
I'm Evil witch. I shall punish you!

317
00:26:03,580 --> 00:26:05,880
Wait a second.

318
00:26:06,620 --> 00:26:07,830
Where are you going?

319
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:11,260
- Stop!
- You can't stop me!

320
00:26:11,670 --> 00:26:13,610
Abracadabra! Got you!

321
00:26:16,760 --> 00:26:19,250
Don't come any closer! I have a magic staff!

322
00:26:32,140 --> 00:26:34,170
After everything they'd been through,

323
00:26:34,370 --> 00:26:36,820
the prince and the princess

324
00:26:37,170 --> 00:26:38,790
finally found their happily ever after

325
00:26:38,980 --> 00:26:40,870
and lived happily ever after.

326
00:27:16,120 --> 00:27:17,410
Sweet dreams.

327
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:44,380
I'm really not available tomorrow.

328
00:27:44,500 --> 00:27:45,680
I'm sorry.

329
00:27:48,020 --> 00:27:50,610
That's okay if you're busy.

330
00:27:50,970 --> 00:27:52,150
Thank you.

331
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:53,730
Okay.

332
00:28:19,040 --> 00:28:20,550
Is Fai asleep?

333
00:28:21,060 --> 00:28:22,960
How was she today? Did she get fussy?

334
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:26,890
Not at all. She fell asleep after just one bedtime story.

335
00:28:28,030 --> 00:28:29,690
But it seems

336
00:28:29,880 --> 00:28:32,110
the fussy one isn't Fai.

337
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:34,540
Come here, good boy.

338
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:38,110
Tell me. Is something wrong?

339
00:28:41,560 --> 00:28:44,810
Actually, I have work tomorrow.

340
00:28:45,220 --> 00:28:47,370
But after Fai came into the picture,

341
00:28:47,820 --> 00:28:49,650
I thought I'd find someone to cover for me.

342
00:28:50,020 --> 00:28:51,020
Mm-hmm.

343
00:28:52,590 --> 00:28:55,610
I called several photographers I know,

344
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:57,690
but none of them were available.

345
00:28:58,040 --> 00:28:59,730
And it's already so late.

346
00:29:00,020 --> 00:29:02,660
I don't see what there is to worry about.

347
00:29:02,950 --> 00:29:06,530
You go to work, and as for Fai,

348
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:08,340
I'll take care of her.

349
00:29:10,160 --> 00:29:12,630
It's okay. I feel bad.

350
00:29:12,830 --> 00:29:14,900
I already promised Aunt Prae.

351
00:29:15,360 --> 00:29:18,200
But you're the one who'll have to go through all the trouble.

352
00:29:19,260 --> 00:29:22,150
Don't overthink it. It's no big deal.

353
00:29:22,420 --> 00:29:26,100
Look at you. You're pouting from worrying too much.

354
00:29:27,120 --> 00:29:27,760
Hmm?

355
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,220
Then...

356
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:35,260
I'll finish work as quickly as I can and come straight back.

357
00:29:36,050 --> 00:29:41,350
No problem. Think of it as a chance for me to practice.

358
00:29:41,690 --> 00:29:42,180
Hmm?

359
00:29:43,600 --> 00:29:44,710
Practice?

360
00:29:45,410 --> 00:29:46,710
Practice what?

361
00:29:47,540 --> 00:29:48,410
Well...

362
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:51,100
Practice being Papa.

363
00:29:51,750 --> 00:29:52,770
P'Fah.

364
00:29:52,920 --> 00:29:53,440
Yeah?

365
00:29:54,590 --> 00:29:57,410
See? You're smiling again.

366
00:29:58,980 --> 00:30:01,000
Were you teasing me?

367
00:30:01,570 --> 00:30:05,100
I just didn't want you to be stressed.

368
00:30:06,870 --> 00:30:08,980
Do you remember what I told you?

369
00:30:09,340 --> 00:30:13,000
That your smile suits you better than anything.

370
00:30:15,610 --> 00:30:18,910
Then let's make a deal.

371
00:30:20,600 --> 00:30:22,520
What kind of deal?

372
00:30:24,550 --> 00:30:28,100
From now on, you're not allowed to solve problems by yourself.

373
00:30:28,300 --> 00:30:30,260
No matter how big or small,

374
00:30:30,680 --> 00:30:33,000
I want you to think of me first.

375
00:30:33,320 --> 00:30:34,420
Okay?

376
00:30:35,020 --> 00:30:37,850
But there are some things I can handle on my own.

377
00:30:37,950 --> 00:30:39,880
No, Phoon.

378
00:30:44,180 --> 00:30:45,650
Okay.

379
00:30:46,090 --> 00:30:47,770
If anything comes up,

380
00:30:47,830 --> 00:30:49,850
I'll tell you everything,

381
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:52,230
and I'll be the first to know.

382
00:30:53,590 --> 00:30:54,340
Mm.

383
00:30:55,670 --> 00:30:57,560
Tell P'Fah first,

384
00:30:57,790 --> 00:31:00,290
and tell him everything.

385
00:31:00,520 --> 00:31:04,780
Good job, Phoon. That's exactly why you're so adorable.
That's right.

386
00:31:07,050 --> 00:31:09,940
It's late. Time for bed.

387
00:31:12,050 --> 00:31:15,400
But I'm not sleepy yet.

388
00:31:16,140 --> 00:31:18,270
Don't try to sweet-talk me.

389
00:31:19,060 --> 00:31:21,040
You spoiled kid.

390
00:31:21,500 --> 00:31:23,280
Go to bed.

391
00:31:27,150 --> 00:31:28,480
Okay.

392
00:31:28,770 --> 00:31:30,050
I'll go to sleep.

393
00:31:32,500 --> 00:31:33,320
Let's go.

394
00:31:54,950 --> 00:31:55,980
Uh...

395
00:31:56,850 --> 00:31:58,120
P'Fah./Phoon.

396
00:32:06,260 --> 00:32:08,670
You go first.

397
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:16,970
It just feels a little strange

398
00:32:17,280 --> 00:32:19,420
not getting to hold you while sleeping tonight.

399
00:32:20,500 --> 00:32:23,460
What about you? What did you want to say?

400
00:32:27,010 --> 00:32:30,190
I feel the same.

401
00:32:47,830 --> 00:32:48,690
Phoon.

402
00:32:50,120 --> 00:32:51,690
What are you doing?

403
00:32:56,690 --> 00:32:58,040
Phoon.

404
00:33:00,240 --> 00:33:02,370
Mind if I snuggle up next to you?

405
00:33:03,780 --> 00:33:05,180
You're more than welcome.

406
00:33:13,810 --> 00:33:14,960
Good night, Phoon.

407
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:18,320
Good night.

408
00:33:36,370 --> 00:33:40,290
It's Sunday. Why does P'Phoon have to work?

409
00:33:40,780 --> 00:33:43,780
My job doesn't have weekends off like school does.

410
00:33:44,270 --> 00:33:47,530
The more days I work, the more snack money I earn.

411
00:33:47,850 --> 00:33:51,160
Then why doesn't P'Fah give P'Phoon money to buy snacks?

412
00:33:51,790 --> 00:33:53,300
Uh...

413
00:33:54,620 --> 00:33:55,920
Good question.

414
00:33:56,480 --> 00:33:59,910
I'm going to be late. I'll hurry back and play with you.

415
00:34:00,340 --> 00:34:03,810
Phoon, are you sure you don't want us to ride you to work?

416
00:34:04,840 --> 00:34:08,020
It's okay. It'll be easier if you stay home.

417
00:34:10,060 --> 00:34:12,680
Be a good girl and stay with P'Fah, okay?

418
00:34:12,970 --> 00:34:15,420
Okay. I'll take care of P'Fah.

419
00:34:17,530 --> 00:34:18,900
Bye.

420
00:34:19,650 --> 00:34:20,590
P'Phoon.

421
00:34:22,600 --> 00:34:23,510
P'Fah.

422
00:34:24,370 --> 00:34:25,470
- I'm off.
- Bye.

423
00:34:25,810 --> 00:34:26,800
Bye.

424
00:34:28,940 --> 00:34:31,230
I'll be back soon.

425
00:34:42,790 --> 00:34:44,840
Come on, let's go inside.

426
00:34:55,380 --> 00:34:57,150
Nice and easy.

427
00:34:57,400 --> 00:34:59,060
That's the mood. Perfect.

428
00:34:59,310 --> 00:35:01,830
Great. Looking good.

429
00:35:01,830 --> 00:35:04,940
Stretch your arms out. That's it.

430
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:08,590
Okay, let me check the photos.

431
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:20,180
How do they look?

432
00:35:24,740 --> 00:35:25,660
Thank you.

433
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:28,400
- Have you eaten yet, P'Phoon?
- I have.

434
00:35:29,160 --> 00:35:30,960
What about you and P'Fah?

435
00:35:31,340 --> 00:35:32,950
We're eating right now.

436
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:35,810
Are you tired, P'Fah?

437
00:35:36,300 --> 00:35:39,190
Not at all. Fai's been such a sweetheart.

438
00:35:39,980 --> 00:35:43,160
- Hurry home, P'Phoon!
- I will.

439
00:35:43,380 --> 00:35:44,780
I'll be home soon.

440
00:35:45,310 --> 00:35:48,080
Oh, P'Fah, I already made dinner.

441
00:35:48,160 --> 00:35:50,020
Just heat it up.

442
00:35:50,860 --> 00:35:54,060
Got it. Come home soon. I miss you.

443
00:35:56,140 --> 00:35:58,280
Bye.

444
00:36:04,180 --> 00:36:05,880
P'Pop, are we all set?

445
00:36:06,070 --> 00:36:08,870
Yes. Let's move, everyone.

446
00:36:09,020 --> 00:36:11,920
Model, please.

447
00:36:27,750 --> 00:36:29,840
Ready? Here we go.

448
00:36:30,700 --> 00:36:33,070
I'm back.

449
00:37:04,010 --> 00:37:05,320
Oh, Phoon.

450
00:37:05,460 --> 00:37:06,910
You're back?

451
00:37:09,260 --> 00:37:11,750
How was it? Tired?

452
00:37:12,200 --> 00:37:13,840
Not at all.

453
00:37:36,160 --> 00:37:37,740
Someone's been naughty.

454
00:37:39,010 --> 00:37:39,860
P'Fah.

455
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:03,880
What are you smiling about?

456
00:38:04,070 --> 00:38:05,580
You've been smiling for a while now.

457
00:38:09,510 --> 00:38:11,150
You're adorable.

458
00:38:19,990 --> 00:38:21,480
Really?

459
00:38:30,370 --> 00:38:33,130
What were you two up to? Why do you look like this?

460
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:38,150
We played dress-up.

461
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:44,700
I've never seen this side of you before.

462
00:38:47,160 --> 00:38:50,070
Well, honestly...

463
00:38:50,420 --> 00:38:52,680
I've never seen this side of myself either.

464
00:38:52,920 --> 00:38:54,210
It's my first time.

465
00:38:58,340 --> 00:38:59,820
It's cute.

466
00:39:02,260 --> 00:39:02,970
Hm?

467
00:39:03,930 --> 00:39:04,670
What was that?

468
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:08,560
P'Fah.

469
00:39:09,540 --> 00:39:12,540
I didn't hear you.

470
00:39:12,750 --> 00:39:13,810
What did you say?

471
00:39:16,690 --> 00:39:18,430
I said...

472
00:39:20,030 --> 00:39:23,530
You're cute from this side too.

473
00:39:24,210 --> 00:39:25,830
Oh.

474
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:28,300
I see.

475
00:39:33,210 --> 00:39:34,360
I missed you.

476
00:39:36,880 --> 00:39:38,480
P'Fah.

477
00:39:39,880 --> 00:39:42,320
Okay, I won't tease you anymore.

478
00:39:43,250 --> 00:39:47,630
By the way, are you taking Fai with me tomorrow?

479
00:39:49,640 --> 00:39:52,640
Yes, then I'll head straight to work.

480
00:39:54,320 --> 00:39:55,440
Okay.

481
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:59,280
I think I'll go take a shower first.

482
00:40:00,460 --> 00:40:01,600
Mm.

483
00:40:02,240 --> 00:40:03,670
Sounds good.

484
00:40:04,110 --> 00:40:05,990
Actually,

485
00:40:06,400 --> 00:40:08,270
I haven't showered yet either.

486
00:40:13,540 --> 00:40:15,740
You go first, P'Fah.

487
00:40:17,640 --> 00:40:19,100
Phoon.

488
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:20,840
Please?

489
00:40:35,640 --> 00:40:36,520
Phoon...

490
00:40:36,770 --> 00:40:38,350
I like you.

491
00:40:39,210 --> 00:40:43,210
But I don't like that mischievous look in your eyes right now.

492
00:40:50,260 --> 00:40:51,190
Phoon.

493
00:41:25,300 --> 00:41:26,750
I love you, Phoon.

494
00:41:47,280 --> 00:41:48,960
- Doesn't it hurt?
- No.

495
00:41:50,980 --> 00:41:53,020
Okay, they're even now.

496
00:41:57,670 --> 00:41:59,170
All done.

497
00:42:01,470 --> 00:42:03,890
Breakfast's ready, you two.

498
00:42:04,780 --> 00:42:06,820
Coming!

499
00:42:07,920 --> 00:42:09,550
- Hungry?
- Yes!

500
00:42:10,050 --> 00:42:10,840
Let's go.

501
00:42:16,160 --> 00:42:18,450
- Can you eat this?
- Yes.

502
00:42:20,500 --> 00:42:22,530
I have some good news today.

503
00:42:25,190 --> 00:42:27,250
After school today,

504
00:42:28,610 --> 00:42:30,280
we're going to pick up your mom.

505
00:42:31,600 --> 00:42:33,130
Did Aunt Prae's test results come out?

506
00:42:33,900 --> 00:42:37,400
Yes. The results showed there's nothing to worry about.

507
00:42:38,490 --> 00:42:41,350
Your mom is going to be healthy again.

508
00:42:42,050 --> 00:42:43,860
Yay!

509
00:42:43,960 --> 00:42:46,330
- Are you happy?
- Very happy!

510
00:42:48,900 --> 00:42:49,810
Fai.

511
00:42:50,210 --> 00:42:51,300
Here, try a bite.

512
00:42:53,430 --> 00:42:55,840
Mm, it's so delicious, P'Phoon!

513
00:42:56,080 --> 00:42:57,790
Finish it all, okay?

514
00:42:57,930 --> 00:42:59,870
- Clean your plate.
- I will!

515
00:43:42,120 --> 00:43:43,360
Yes, P'Fah?

516
00:43:44,420 --> 00:43:46,760
Hey, little one. Are you off work yet?

517
00:43:47,040 --> 00:43:48,490
Not yet. A little while longer.

518
00:43:48,850 --> 00:43:52,060
But it's almost time for Fai to get out of school, right?

519
00:43:52,540 --> 00:43:53,550
That's right.

520
00:43:54,340 --> 00:43:58,430
I'll pick Fai up first, then I'll call you.

521
00:43:59,640 --> 00:44:00,940
And...

522
00:44:01,960 --> 00:44:03,960
How's Aunt Prae doing?

523
00:44:04,760 --> 00:44:06,180
Everything's all set.

524
00:44:06,400 --> 00:44:08,690
I've already settled her into her room.

525
00:44:10,210 --> 00:44:12,390
Thanks for taking care of everything.

526
00:44:14,950 --> 00:44:16,280
I love you, P'Fah.

527
00:44:17,050 --> 00:44:19,330
I love you too.

528
00:44:27,660 --> 00:44:29,120
This one looks great.

529
00:44:29,360 --> 00:44:31,200
See you.

530
00:44:31,560 --> 00:44:33,210
See you on the next shoot.

531
00:44:39,040 --> 00:44:40,240
Typhoon.

532
00:44:43,590 --> 00:44:45,550
Your photos turned out amazing today.

533
00:44:45,670 --> 00:44:49,040
- Thanks.
- I'd like to exchange contact information.

534
00:44:49,570 --> 00:44:52,150
Maybe we can work together again sometime.

535
00:44:53,860 --> 00:44:54,910
Oh, sure.

536
00:44:55,040 --> 00:44:57,470
I really loved today's shoot,

537
00:44:57,640 --> 00:45:00,840
so I'd like to treat the crew to dinner. Want to join us?

538
00:45:03,420 --> 00:45:04,720
Uh...

539
00:45:06,860 --> 00:45:08,530
Well...

540
00:45:14,740 --> 00:45:15,560
Phoon.

541
00:45:31,050 --> 00:45:32,410
We're here to pick you up.

542
00:45:37,470 --> 00:45:40,840
Thanks for liking my work, but I'm really not available today.

543
00:45:41,240 --> 00:45:43,980
- I'll get going then.
- Sure.

544
00:45:47,240 --> 00:45:48,180
Hello.

545
00:45:48,940 --> 00:45:49,620
Hi.

546
00:45:52,360 --> 00:45:55,030
Little one, shall we get going?

547
00:45:55,230 --> 00:45:56,790
We don't want to keep Aunt Prae waiting.

548
00:46:05,900 --> 00:46:07,710
- Let's go.
- Okay.

549
00:47:03,380 --> 00:47:05,370
Mom!

550
00:47:08,780 --> 00:47:11,730
- I missed you so much.
- I missed you too, Mom.

551
00:47:14,410 --> 00:47:17,050
I have to thank you both again.

552
00:47:18,300 --> 00:47:20,200
I've spoken with the attending physician.

553
00:47:20,330 --> 00:47:22,850
Your test results look very reassuring.

554
00:47:23,260 --> 00:47:25,990
I'm just so relieved it's not cancer.

555
00:47:26,460 --> 00:47:29,610
Thank you too, Tonfah. You've done so much for me.

556
00:47:29,880 --> 00:47:31,720
It's my pleasure. Not at all.

557
00:47:31,930 --> 00:47:34,820
But please make sure to keep your follow-up appointments.

558
00:47:35,740 --> 00:47:39,170
Thank you again, Phoon and Tonfah.

559
00:47:40,960 --> 00:47:44,270
If there's ever anything I can do, just let me know.

560
00:47:45,220 --> 00:47:48,430
And bring Fai over to our place whenever you're free.

561
00:47:48,600 --> 00:47:50,140
We'd love to.

562
00:47:50,970 --> 00:47:53,440
Oh, there's something I'd like to ask.

563
00:47:53,980 --> 00:47:56,570
About the medical expenses.

564
00:47:57,760 --> 00:47:58,840
Well...

565
00:48:01,610 --> 00:48:05,440
Besides being a doctor,

566
00:48:05,600 --> 00:48:09,070
P'Fah also happens to own the hospital.

567
00:48:09,890 --> 00:48:13,880
Goodness! Tonfah, you really own this hospital?

568
00:48:14,320 --> 00:48:17,090
Please don't worry. I'd be happy to take care of it.

569
00:48:18,600 --> 00:48:22,370
We should get going now.

570
00:48:22,660 --> 00:48:25,980
Thank you so much, Tonfah and Typhoon.

571
00:48:31,280 --> 00:48:32,870
Come visit P'Fah's house again.

572
00:48:33,320 --> 00:48:35,000
Okay!

573
00:48:35,890 --> 00:48:38,930
- Take care.
- I will.

574
00:48:46,120 --> 00:48:48,620
I'm so happy to see Typhoon happy.

575
00:48:48,830 --> 00:48:51,070
And with such a wonderful family.

576
00:48:51,610 --> 00:48:52,590
Thank you.

577
00:48:54,510 --> 00:48:56,520
Please take good care of him, Tonfah.

578
00:48:57,450 --> 00:48:59,300
I will, Aunt Prae.

579
00:49:01,430 --> 00:49:03,340
We really have to go now.

580
00:49:03,520 --> 00:49:08,390
- Fai, say goodbye.
- Goodbye, P'Fah. Goodbye, P'Phoon.

581
00:49:08,890 --> 00:49:09,960
Let's go.

582
00:49:56,220 --> 00:49:58,190
You're still working?

583
00:50:00,870 --> 00:50:02,290
Who was that guy?

584
00:50:02,950 --> 00:50:04,770
Was he bothering you?

585
00:50:07,830 --> 00:50:09,040
Who?

586
00:50:10,860 --> 00:50:12,500
That man.

587
00:50:12,930 --> 00:50:14,880
The one I saw talking to you.

588
00:50:16,940 --> 00:50:19,710
He's just a client who hired me for today's shoot.

589
00:50:22,250 --> 00:50:22,970
But...

590
00:50:23,730 --> 00:50:26,780
I saw you talking to him for quite a while.

591
00:50:27,460 --> 00:50:28,640
What were you talking about?

592
00:50:30,480 --> 00:50:32,950
He just invited me to dinner.

593
00:50:36,390 --> 00:50:37,790
Dinner?

594
00:50:40,090 --> 00:50:41,960
He said

595
00:50:42,320 --> 00:50:46,920
he really liked my work and wanted to treat the crew to dinner.

596
00:50:53,050 --> 00:50:56,900
Will you have to work with him again?

597
00:51:17,460 --> 00:51:19,350
P'Fah.

598
00:51:20,220 --> 00:51:21,520
Are you jealous?

599
00:51:22,820 --> 00:51:23,490
Hmm?

600
00:51:26,000 --> 00:51:27,130
Yes.

601
00:51:27,940 --> 00:51:28,850
I am.

602
00:51:30,020 --> 00:51:31,760
And I'm very possessive, too.

603
00:51:38,980 --> 00:51:42,260
I only love you, P'Fah.

604
00:51:42,900 --> 00:51:45,990
No matter how many more people come into this world,

605
00:51:47,180 --> 00:51:49,770
I'll only ever love you.

606
00:51:54,090 --> 00:51:57,400
I really only love you, P'Fah.

607
00:52:02,880 --> 00:52:04,590
After hearing you say all that,

608
00:52:05,020 --> 00:52:06,710
what am I supposed to do?

609
00:52:10,400 --> 00:52:11,800
I love you too.

610
00:52:16,070 --> 00:52:17,460
Very much.

611
00:52:22,200 --> 00:52:23,350
I really do.

612
00:52:26,610 --> 00:52:28,080
P'Fah.

613
00:52:29,100 --> 00:52:31,620
I was just afraid you wouldn't believe me.

614
00:52:37,960 --> 00:52:39,440
It's time to sleep.

615
00:52:42,300 --> 00:52:43,360
But...

616
00:52:49,400 --> 00:52:50,490
Alright.

617
00:53:12,460 --> 00:53:13,820
Good night, Phoon.

618
00:53:14,400 --> 00:53:15,630
Good night.

619
00:53:37,500 --> 00:53:38,560
Phoon.

620
00:53:41,160 --> 00:53:42,850
Where are you, Phoon?

621
00:53:47,920 --> 00:53:49,070
Phoon.

622
00:55:16,850 --> 00:55:20,280
Happy 6th anniversary, my sky.

623
00:55:26,670 --> 00:55:29,960
Did you prepare this surprise for me, little one?

624
00:55:32,020 --> 00:55:33,160
Do you like it?

625
00:55:48,710 --> 00:55:50,430
I love it more than anything.

626
00:55:53,330 --> 00:55:55,720
Mm. I...

627
00:55:56,780 --> 00:55:58,820
have something for you too.

628
00:56:15,180 --> 00:56:17,990
Happy 6th anniversary to you too.

629
00:56:19,190 --> 00:56:21,190
P'Fah.

630
00:56:21,450 --> 00:56:24,210
Here, let me put it on you.

631
00:56:44,420 --> 00:56:45,910
There.

632
00:56:57,880 --> 00:56:59,120
Phoon.

633
00:57:06,840 --> 00:57:08,080
Thank you.

634
00:57:10,520 --> 00:57:13,670
Thank you for becoming the best thing in my life.

635
00:57:16,290 --> 00:57:18,070
I'm so glad I get to love you.

636
00:57:20,160 --> 00:57:22,640
I'm so glad I get to love you too.

637
00:58:06,650 --> 00:58:10,284
You've kept all of these, Phoon?
That's so cute.

638
00:58:10,330 --> 00:58:11,590
Yes.
